            "is_markdown": false,
            "count": 0,
            "bug_id": 19292,
            "text": "do_chartr() (src/main/character.c) counts the entries of its wide-character translation table in an int. A valid UTF-8 'old' spec whose ranges total exactly 2^32 entries wraps that count to 0, R_alloc() returns a one-entry table, and the loop that fills the table writes four billion entries past it. Any multibyte locale reaches this path, and the spec is 23 KB of ordinary valid UTF-8 (3855 full Unicode ranges plus one of 69391 code points). R 4.5.3 segfaults after about 7 s.\n\nReproducible example: attached as chartr-table-count-repro.R; segfaults, expected an error.\n\nAnalysis:\n\nThe count loop increments xtable_cnt (int) once per expanded entry, so 2^32 entries leave it at 0 and R_alloc(xtable_cnt+1, sizeof(xtable_t)) allocates a single entry; the fill loop is indexed by R_xlen_t and writes all 2^32. Tested at r90850.\n\nProposed patch: attached as chartr-table-count.diff. It counts in R_xlen_t and refuses a spec that expands to more than INT_MAX entries, which is what the int indices and the sort macros can address anyway; the spec above now errors with \"'old' expands to too many characters\". No regression test, since the reproducer walks four billion entries and takes several seconds even in a release build.\n\nThe patch is also submitted as https://github.com/r-devel/r-svn/pull/458, where CI results can be seen."
          },
